---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro'
import Footer from '../components/Footer.astro'
---

<BaseLayout
  currentPath="/about/"
  title="About TRACED | Jonathan R. Reed Data Breach Archive Project"
  description="Learn how Jonathan R. Reed built TRACED as a static public breach archive using Have I Been Pwned data, client-side password checking, and privacy-first design."
>

  <main id="main-content" tabindex="-1" class="page">
    <header class="page-head band">
      <h1>About TRACED</h1>
      <p class="lede">
        TRACED is a weekend project. I wanted a better way to browse the
        <a href="https://haveibeenpwned.com" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Have I Been Pwned<span class="sr-only"> (opens in a new tab)</span></a>
        dataset: one long list you can search, and a case file for every breach.
      </p>
      <p class="byline">
        <img
          src="https://img.jonathanrreed.com/personal/jonathan.avif"
          alt=""
          width="48"
          height="48"
          class="byline-photo"
          onerror="this.style.display='none'"
        />
        <span>
          By <a href="https://jonathanrreed.com" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Jonathan R. Reed<span class="sr-only"> (opens in a new tab)</span></a>
        </span>
      </p>
    </header>
    <div class="wrap about">

      <div class="prose">
        <section>
          <h2>What this is</h2>
          <p>
            A browser for the Have I Been Pwned breach database. Each breach gets its own case file with the breach
            date, the number of affected accounts, the data that was exposed, and when HIBP added it to the database.
          </p>
          <p>
            It doesn't replace HIBP. It's another way to read public breach history, and a reminder that old accounts
            tend to outlive the services they were made for.
          </p>
        </section>

        <section>
          <h2>How to read it</h2>
          <dl class="how">
            <div>
              <dt><span class="leak-hot">*</span>Marked data types</dt>
              <dd>
                Passwords, financial details, government IDs, health data and private messages are printed in red
                with an asterisk. They are the ones that change what you should do next, and the list can be filtered
                by them.
              </dd>
            </div>
            <div>
              <dt>Accounts</dt>
              <dd>
                The number of account records in a breach, as HIBP counts them. One person can appear in many
                breaches, so the total across the list is records, not people.
              </dd>
            </div>
            <div>
              <dt>HIBP listing interval</dt>
              <dd>
                The time between the recorded breach date and when HIBP added it to the database. It does not tell
                you when the breach was discovered or publicly disclosed.
              </dd>
            </div>
          </dl>
        </section>

        <section>
          <h2>How it works</h2>
          <dl class="how">
            <div>
              <dt>Pre-built pages</dt>
              <dd>
                Every breach page is generated at build time from HIBP's public breach feed. No app server or database
                sits behind it.
              </dd>
            </div>
            <div>
              <dt>No tracking</dt>
              <dd>
                No analytics, no cookies and no behavioral tracking. TRACED adds no logging or profiling of its own.
                Hosting providers may keep standard request logs.
              </dd>
            </div>
            <div>
              <dt>Password check</dt>
              <dd>
                Your browser hashes the password and sends only the first 5 characters of the hash. The password itself
                never leaves your device.
              </dd>
            </div>
          </dl>
        </section>

        <section>
          <h2>Data sources</h2>
          <p>
            Everything here comes from Troy Hunt's Have I Been Pwned, a public breach database he has run since 2013.
          </p>

          <div class="sources">
            <article class="source">
              <h3>Have I Been Pwned</h3>
              <p>
                The main breach database. Every publicly known breach, with dates, the number of affected accounts,
                the data taken and whether the breach is verified. Free, no API key.
              </p>
              <ul class="endpoints data">
                <li>GET haveibeenpwned.com/api/v3/breaches</li>
                <li>GET haveibeenpwned.com/api/v3/breach/{'{name}'}</li>
              </ul>
              <a href="https://haveibeenpwned.com" target="_blank" rel="noopener">haveibeenpwned.com<span class="sr-only"> (opens in a new tab)</span></a>
            </article>

            <article class="source">
              <h3>Pwned Passwords</h3>
              <p>
                Hundreds of millions of real passwords exposed in past breaches. The password checker uses this API
                with k-anonymity, so the full password or hash is never sent.
              </p>
              <ul class="endpoints data">
                <li>GET api.pwnedpasswords.com/range/{'{prefix}'}</li>
              </ul>
              <a href="https://haveibeenpwned.com/Passwords" target="_blank" rel="noopener">haveibeenpwned.com/Passwords<span class="sr-only"> (opens in a new tab)</span></a>
            </article>
          </div>

          <p class="muted">
            All the data belongs to Troy Hunt and Have I Been Pwned. TRACED is an independent front end, not affiliated
            with or endorsed by HIBP.
          </p>
        </section>

        <section>
          <h2>Built with</h2>
          <p>
            Astro 7 for the static pages, React 19 for the interactive parts, Tailwind CSS v4 and
            <a href="https://starwind.dev" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Starwind UI<span class="sr-only"> (opens in a new tab)</span></a>
            for styling and components, and Cloudflare Pages for hosting. The type is Martian Mono, Doto and
            Atkinson Hyperlegible, all served from this domain.
          </p>
        </section>
      </div>
    </div>
  </main>
  <Footer />
</BaseLayout>

<style>
  .byline {
    display: flex;
    align-items: center;
    gap: 0.75rem;
    color: var(--ink-soft);
  }

  .byline-photo {
    width: 3rem;
    height: 3rem;
    border-radius: 50%;
    object-fit: cover;
    border: 1px solid var(--rule);
  }

  .how {
    display: grid;
    gap: 1.25rem;
    margin: 0;
  }

  .how dt {
    font-family: var(--font-display);
    font-stretch: var(--display-stretch);
    font-weight: 700;
    letter-spacing: -0.02em;
  }

  .how dd {
    margin: 0.15rem 0 0;
    color: var(--ink-soft);
  }

  .sources {
    display: grid;
    gap: 1.5rem;
  }

  .source {
    display: grid;
    gap: 0.6rem;
  }

  .source p {
    color: var(--ink-soft);
  }

  .endpoints {
    display: grid;
    margin: 0;
    padding: 0;
    list-style: none;
    word-break: break-all;
  }

  .endpoints li {
    padding: 0.45rem 0.75rem;
  }

  .endpoints li:nth-child(odd) {
    background: var(--bar);
  }
</style>
